<title>CANADA: Canada government cash balances rise in week.</title>
<headline>Canada government cash balances rise in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances rose in the week that ended April 2, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>				    Wk to Apr 2  Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  27.11   -0.100    +0.596</p>
<p>Government cash balances	    11.28   +4.205    +1.735</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	466.31   +3.878    +4.036</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 135.40   +3.800   -30.700</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  32.90   -0.043    +2.157</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>					   Feb 97     Jan 97     Feb 96</p>
<p>M1					  68.59	68.71	58.48</p>
<p>M2					 392.19     394.81     386.93</p>
<p>M3					 499.91     497.81     473.39</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			 Feb	   Jan</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-19.81	-16.27</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     692.64	685.17</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    105.81	105.23</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
</text>
